\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.5}{\ignorespaces Decomposition of CAA vectors into a shared emotionalisation component $\mathbf  {g}$ and emotion-specific residuals $\mathbf  {r}_e$. The original pooled CAA vector $\mathbf  {c}_e$ is the sum of these two components. This decomposition reveals that while the dominant structure is a common shift towards emotionality, there is also a structured residual geometry that encodes specific emotion identities.}}{25}{figure.caption.50}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:caa_decomposition_schematic}{{3.5}{25}{Decomposition of CAA vectors into a shared emotionalisation component $\mathbf {g}$ and emotion-specific residuals $\mathbf {r}_e$. The original pooled CAA vector $\mathbf {c}_e$ is the sum of these two components. This decomposition reveals that while the dominant structure is a common shift towards emotionality, there is also a structured residual geometry that encodes specific emotion identities}{figure.caption.50}{}}
